From e6d2f7005995f9739110043b5457a3aac54eb654 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ymote <151983+ymote@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:44:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(shell): host the octoscode module (app-octoscode)

Link OctosCode, the native octos client of the octoscode-app repository,
into the shell as an in-process module, opt-in like AppCard:

- root Cargo.toml: apps/octoscode/{client,store,module} are workspace
  members and path dependencies (the octoscode repo vendors its crates
  there, with its design/ in apps/design, at build time); `publish` joins
  [workspace.package] (the crates inherit it); `octoscript-widgets` joins
  [workspace.dependencies]; the Octoscript-Makepad [patch] points at the
  octoscode repo's renderer fork, beside this tree
  (../octoscript-makepad-fork: this rev + its patches/octoscript-makepad,
  which add to_makepad_ui_in_slot, the module's mount path).
- crates/shell: the optional `octoscode-module` dependency and the feature
  `app-octoscode = ["dep:octoscode-module", "app-hub", "octos-core"]`;
  linked_modules() pushes OCTOSCODE_MODULE under it, next to AppCard.
- desktop/, phone/: the feature forwarded (`app-octoscode`).
- apps/appcard/app: l0_eval.rs fills `padright`, the field the renderer
  fork adds to octoscript_node's Attrs beside its four padding siblings
  (without it the fork does not compile here).
- Cargo.lock: the three crates and the shell's new dependency. Every
  dependency they use is already pinned by this lock, so a fresh tree
  builds exactly this graph and `cargo build --locked` passes.

Build: cargo build -p octosense --features app-octoscode; run with
MAKEPAD_WM_TEST_APP=octoscode ... --module octoscode. The octoscode repo's
tools/build-macos.sh --octosense prepares the whole tree (this patch is its
patches/octosense/0003, applied after 0001 and 0002 by
tools/prepare-octosense-fork.sh).
